# ======================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT INVENTORY -- NOT A REPRODUCIBLE INSTALLATION LOCKFILE
#
# This file records the packages observed (via `python -m pip freeze`) inside
# the EXISTING local Docker images during the F0A read-only baseline on
# 2026-11-23. It documents what the verified images contain. Do not use it as
# `pip install -r` input and do not treat it as pinned or hash-locked:
#   * it carries no --hash entries and no index information;
#   * torch is a local-version build (+cpu) that is only served by the PyTorch
#     CPU index, not PyPI;
#   * a clean rebuild from Dockerfile.level5 / requirements-level5.txt was
#     observed to differ from these images (base-image layer, and the
#     unpinned transitive packages cloudpickle, narwhals, threadpoolctl).
# Dependency installation behaviour is unchanged by this file. A real,
# hash-locked lockfile is a separate later milestone.
#
# Platform for every image below: linux/amd64, Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie),
# Python 3.15.2, PYTHONHASHSEED=42.
# ======================================================================

